00:54:06.520 --> 00:54:10.600
But, I didn't go on any 9D rides.

00:54:10.600 --> 00:54:17.940
But, I did walk by a casino that has been abandoned for, I think, maybe 15, 10, 10, 15 years.

00:54:18.520 --> 00:54:19.760
And, it is spooky.

00:54:20.220 --> 00:54:23.460
I don't think we walked past any spooky abandons.

00:54:24.320 --> 00:54:30.240
There were definitely more open casinos when we were there.

00:54:30.480 --> 00:54:34.060
Yeah, when we were there, the Trump Taj Mahal was still around.

00:54:34.060 --> 00:54:37.000
Yeah, I think that's where we went for most of our gambling.

00:54:38.200 --> 00:54:42.800
I've never considered, like, what an abandoned casino would look like inside.

00:54:43.040 --> 00:54:45.920
Oh, it's just, like, especially if you walk by it at night.

00:54:45.920 --> 00:54:52.160
And, especially if, maybe just coincidentally, the boardwalk lights also don't work in front of that casino.

00:54:54.020 --> 00:54:55.000
Yeah, that's eerie.

00:54:55.000 --> 00:54:56.800
It's kind of terrifying, yeah.

00:54:56.860 --> 00:54:59.380
It's, like, eerie in a way that I've never thought of before.

00:55:02.180 --> 00:55:04.520
Yes, it's pretty spooky.

00:55:04.520 --> 00:55:10.120
Now, there are obviously a ton to talk about when it comes to the video games, too.

00:55:10.260 --> 00:55:14.400
Not just all the variants of the board game and other places Monopoly has shown up.

00:55:14.520 --> 00:55:19.320
But, more interesting than maybe any port I'm going to tell you about because there's so many ports.

00:55:20.700 --> 00:55:27.820
It's, this version of Monopoly, we're hitting that time now because the Super Nintendo is out.

00:55:27.820 --> 00:55:33.600
We're hitting that time where the, what am I trying to say here?

00:55:33.740 --> 00:55:37.900
The video games are coming out on the NES and the Super Nintendo.

00:55:37.900 --> 00:55:44.220
And so, this same game is available in 16-bit on the Super NES.

00:55:44.900 --> 00:55:47.180
Wait, when did we cross that threshold?

00:55:47.660 --> 00:55:49.740
Well, no, it hasn't happened in America yet.

00:55:49.740 --> 00:55:58.540
But, if you'll recall, in late 1990, we did that, our first Nostalgia episode for Nostalgia Bites.

00:55:58.800 --> 00:56:05.140
And that was to coincide with the release of where it marked in our Nostalgia chronological order.

00:56:05.500 --> 00:56:12.960
Got it. So, in September of 1992, this game, this same exact game will come out in 16-bit here in North America.

00:56:13.560 --> 00:56:15.760
And it also came out on the Genesis.

00:56:16.880 --> 00:56:23.480
And, believe it or not, a Game Boy version, which allows you to use a Game Link cable to connect two Game Boys together.

00:56:23.680 --> 00:56:25.720
So that each, so you can have two player.

00:56:26.820 --> 00:56:31.140
But, I did go out, I had to go out of my way and check out the Super Nintendo version.

00:56:31.480 --> 00:56:34.900
Just to see, like, you know, how much better could it be.

00:56:34.900 --> 00:56:39.960
And I'm here to report, it's exactly the same game, just with nicer graphics.

00:56:40.280 --> 00:56:42.920
A little bit more bit depth in the color palette.

00:56:43.440 --> 00:56:45.160
Yep, that's it, buddy.

00:56:45.400 --> 00:56:46.220
Nothing else.

00:56:46.580 --> 00:56:50.000
It doesn't take this game down a peg.

00:56:50.000 --> 00:56:54.060
If you only own an NES, you're fine with this version of Monopoly.

00:56:54.660 --> 00:57:00.200
There were, though, two other Super Famicom Monopoly games.

